, node_id}` (mounted under `/api`). |\n| `huddle/__main__.py` | `uvicorn` entry: `python -m huddle` reads settings and serves `huddle.app:create_app`. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `.gitignore` | Ignore `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`, `data/*` runtime artifacts (keep `data/.gitkeep` if added), `.timer_start`; do **not** ignore `start.sh` or `huddle/`. |\n| (optional) `data/.gitkeep` | Ensure `/app/data` exists in the tree. |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|---|---|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer; unrelated. |\n| `loom-prompts/` | Agent prompts; not product. |\n\n---ACCEPTANCE---\n\n\n1. `test -x /app/start.sh` (or `./start.sh` in repo root) succeeds.\n2. After starting `./start.sh` (under `marathon-portlock` when ports might be contested) and waiting for readiness:\n   - `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` → HTTP 200, JSON `status==\"ok\"`, `node_id==0`\n   - same for `:8001` → `node_id==1`\n   - same for `:8002` → `node_id==2`\n3. `redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING` → `PONG`.\n4. `start.sh` remains in the foreground (does not daemonize itself and return immediately).\n5. `node_id` values are JSON numbers; response contains no requirement for other keys.\n6. Killing one node’s PID (SIGKILL) does **not** take down the other two health endpoints; within 60s the killed port serves health again with the **same** `node_id`.\n7. Killing `redis-server` does **not** cause health endpoints to fail; Redis accepts `PING` again after `start.sh` respawns it.\n8. No Docker socket usage; no calls to external network services required for health.\n9. A clear module path exists for adding routes (e.g. empty aggregation point in `huddle/api/__init__.py`) so MARATHON-3 can attach `/api/auth/*` without changing `start.sh`.\n10. Negative: binding must **not** use `0.0.0.0` for the three HTTP nodes (must be `127.0.0.1`).\n11. Negative: `/api/health` must **not** return `5xx` solely because Redis is down.\n12. Negative: `node_id` for port 8000 must **not** be `1` or `2` under any restart ordering.\n\n","stderr":"","executionTime":95,"interleavedOutput":"Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `start.sh` | Executable foreground supervisor: deps/venv, Redis, three nodes, restart loop, signal handling. |\n| `requirements.txt` | Pin `fastapi`, `uvicorn[standard]` (and leave room for `redis`, etc. later or add `redis` now unused). Prefer exact pins. |\n| `vendor/` (optional but recommended) | Bundled wheels so `pip install --no-index` works offline. |\n| `huddle/__init__.py` | Package marker; version string optional. |\n| `huddle/config.py` | Read/validate `HUDDLE_*` env; expose `settings.node_id`, `settings.port`, `settings.host`, `settings.redis_url`, `settings.data_dir`. |\n| `huddle/app.py` | `create_app()` → FastAPI instance; include API router; no business routes beyond what’s included. |\n| `huddle/api/__init__.py` | Aggregate `api_router`; include health; comment/marker for sibling routers. |\n| `huddle/api/health.py` | `GET /health` → `{status, node_id}` (mounted under `/api`). |\n| `huddle/__main__.py` | `uvicorn` entry: `python -m huddle` reads settings and serves `huddle.app:create_app`. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `.gitignore` | Ignore `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`, `data/*` runtime artifacts (keep `data/.gitkeep` if added), `.timer_start`; do **not** ignore `start.sh` or `huddle/`. |\n| (optional) `data/.gitkeep` | Ensure `/app/data` exists in the tree. |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|---|---|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer; unrelated. |\n| `loom-prompts/` | Agent prompts; not product. |\n\n---ACCEPTANCE---\n\n\n1. `test -x /app/start.sh` (or `./start.sh` in repo root) succeeds.\n2. After starting `./start.sh` (under `marathon-portlock` when ports might be contested) and waiting for readiness:\n   - `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` → HTTP 200, JSON `status==\"ok\"`, `node_id==0`\n   - same for `:8001` → `node_id==1`\n   - same for `:8002` → `node_id==2`\n3. `redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING` → `PONG`.\n4. `start.sh` remains in the foreground (does not daemonize itself and return immediately).\n5. `node_id` values are JSON numbers; response contains no requirement for other keys.\n6. Killing one node’s PID (SIGKILL) does **not** take down the other two health endpoints; within 60s the killed port serves health again with the **same** `node_id`.\n7. Killing `redis-server` does **not** cause health endpoints to fail; Redis accepts `PING` again after `start.sh` respawns it.\n8. No Docker socket usage; no calls to external network services required for health.\n9. A clear module path exists for adding routes (e.g. empty aggregation point in `huddle/api/__init__.py`) so MARATHON-3 can attach `/api/auth/*` without changing `start.sh`.\n10. Negative: binding must **not** use `0.0.0.0` for the three HTTP nodes (must be `127.0.0.1`).\n11. Negative: `/api/health` must **not** return `5xx` solely because Redis is down.\n12. Negative: `node_id` for port 8000 must **not** be `1` or `2` under any restart ordering.\n\n","localExecutionTimeMs":46},"isBackground":false},"description":"Extract files and acceptance criteria"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-fdb9b6d9-baee-4d05-8cc7-ed4192265caf-7\nfc_8a59ed43-19c2-9bfd-84d3-a6e98a2e30e3_1","startedAtMs":"1787424335605","completedAtMs":"1787424335700"},"model_call_id":"507115f0-fb9b-4c24-8b3e-645abf4e560c-2-iad3","session_id":"15abacc6-9531-4e57-8c31-24c1bdbac2cf","timestamp_ms":1787424335720}
