{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-5\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_2","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"git log --oneline -10 -- start.sh; echo '---'; git status; echo '---'; git log --oneline -5; echo '---comments raw---'; loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null | head -c 2000; loom data comments MARATHON-21 2>/dev/null || true; loom data show MARATHON-21 2>&1 | head -80","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-5\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_2","simpleCommands":["git","echo","git","echo","git","echo","loom","python3","head","loom","true","loom","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"log"},{"type":"word","value":"--oneline"},{"type":"number","value":"-10"},{"type":"word","value":"--"},{"type":"word","value":"start.sh"}],"fullText":"git log --oneline -10 -- start.sh"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"status"}],"fullText":"git status"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"log"},{"type":"word","value":"--oneline"},{"type":"number","value":"-5"}],"fullText":"git log --oneline -5"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---comments raw---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---comments raw---'"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-m"},{"type":"word","value":"json.tool"}],"fullText":"python3 -m json.tool"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"2000"}],"fullText":"head -c 2000"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"comments"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"}],"fullText":"loom data comments MARATHON-21"},{"name":"true","args":[],"fullText":"true"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-21"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-80"}],"fullText":"head -80"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Git history and task comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"49ffb699-fd37-4b50-96be-46bad2e3f892","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Git history and task comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-5\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_2","startedAtMs":"1787424980155"},"model_call_id":"e1004229-730f-4840-966d-b932d594bc6c-1-366j","session_id":"49ffb699-fd37-4b50-96be-46bad2e3f892","timestamp_ms":1787424980181}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-4\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1/start.sh"},"result":{"success":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Huddle cluster supervisor: local Redis + three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nAPP_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$APP_ROOT\"\n\nexport HUDDLE_HOST=\"${HUDDLE_HOST:-127.0.0.1}\"\nexport HUDDLE_REDIS_URL=\"${HUDDLE_REDIS_URL:-redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0}\"\nexport HUDDLE_DATA_DIR=\"${HUDDLE_DATA_DIR:-$APP_ROOT/data}\"\n\nDATA_DIR=\"$HUDDLE_DATA_DIR\"\nREDIS_DIR=\"$DATA_DIR/redis\"\nVENV_DIR=\"$APP_ROOT/.venv\"\nPYTHON_BIN=\"${PYTHON_BIN:-python3}\"\n\nREDIS_PID=\"\"\ndeclare -A NODE_PIDS=()\n\nlog() {\n  printf '[huddle] %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2\n}\n\ndie() {\n  log \"ERROR: $*\"\n  exit 1\n}\n\nport_in_use() {\n  local port=\"$1\"\n  if command -v ss >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    ss -ltn \"sport = :$port\" 2>/dev/null | grep -q \":$port\"\n  else\n    # Fallback: try binding via python\n    \"$PYTHON_BIN\" -c \"import socket;s=socket.socket();s.bind(('127.0.0.1',$port))\" 2>/dev/null && return 1 || return 0\n  fi\n}\n\nensure_deps() {\n  if ! command -v redis-server >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    die \"redis-server binary not found in PATH\"\n  fi\n  if ! command -v \"$PYTHON_BIN\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    die \"python3 not found\"\n  fi\n\n  mkdir -p \"$DATA_DIR\" \"$REDIS_DIR\"\n\n  if [[ ! -d \"$VENV_DIR\" ]]; then\n    log \"Creating virtualenv at $VENV_DIR\"\n    \"$PYTHON_BIN\" -m venv \"$VENV_DIR\"\n  fi\n  # shellcheck disable=SC1091\n  source \"$VENV_DIR/bin/activate\"\n\n  if ! python -c \"import fastapi, uvicorn\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    log \"Installing Python dependencies from vendor/ (offline preferred)\"\n    if [[ -d \"$APP_ROOT/vendor\" ]] && compgen -G \"$APP_ROOT/vendor/*.whl\" >/dev/null; then\n      pip install --no-index --find-links=\"$APP_ROOT/vendor\" -r \"$APP_ROOT/requirements.txt\"\n    else\n      pip install -r \"$APP_ROOT/requirements.txt\"\n    fi\n  fi\n}\n\ncheck_http_ports_free() {\n  local port\n  for port in 8000 8001 8002; do\n    if port_in_use \"$port\"; then\n      die \"Port 127.0.0.1:$port is already in use\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n\nstart_redis() {\n  if redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING 2>/dev/null | grep -q PONG; then\n    log \"Reusing existing Redis on 127.0.0.1:6379\"\n    REDIS_PID=\"\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  if port_in_use 6379; then\n    die \"Port 127.0.0.1:6379 is in use but Redis PING failed\"\n  fi\n  log \"Starting redis-server on 127.0.0.1:6379\"\n  redis-server \\\n    --bind 127.0.0.1 \\\n    --port 6379 \\\n    --dir \"$REDIS_DIR\" \\\n    --daemonize no \\\n    --protected-mode yes \\\n    --save \"\" \\\n    --appendonly no \\\n    >/dev/null 2>&1 &\n  REDIS_PID=$!\n  local i\n  for i in $(seq 1 50); do\n    if redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING 2>/dev/null | grep -q PONG; then\n      log \"Redis ready (pid=${REDIS_PID:-external})\"\n      return 0\n    fi\n    sleep 0.1\n  done\n  die \"Redis failed to become ready\"\n}\n\nstart_node() {\n  local node_id=\"$1\"\n  local port=\"$2\"\n  log \"Starting HTTP node_id=$node_id on 127.0.0.1:$port\"\n  (\n    export HUDDLE_NODE_ID=\"$node_id\"\n    export HUDDLE_PORT=\"$port\"\n    export HUDDLE_HOST\n    export HUDDLE_REDIS_URL\n    export HUDDLE_DATA_DIR\n    exec python -m huddle\n  ) &\n  NODE_PIDS[$node_id]=$!\n}\n\nstop_children() {\n  local pid node_id\n  for node_id in \"${!NODE_PIDS[@]}\"; do\n    pid=\"${NODE_PIDS[$node_id]:-}\"\n    if [[ -n \"$pid\" ]] && kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      kill \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    fi\n  done\n  if [[ -n \"${REDIS_PID:-}\" ]] && kill -0 \"$REDIS_PID\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    kill \"$REDIS_PID\" 2>/dev/null || true\n  fi\n  wait 2>/dev/null || true\n}\n\non_signal() {\n  log \"Shutting down cluster...\"\n  stop_children\n  exit 0\n}\n\ntrap on_signal INT TERM\n\nensure_deps\ncheck_http_ports_free\nstart_redis\n\nstart_node 0 8000\nstart_node 1 8001\nstart_node 2 8002\n\nlog \"Cluster running (foreground). Nodes: ${NODE_PIDS[*]}; redis_pid=${REDIS_PID:-reused}\"\n\n# Supervisor loop: restart dead children; stay in foreground.\nwhile true; do\n  # Redis\n  if ! redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING 2>/dev/null | grep -q PONG; then\n    log \"Redis not responding; restarting\"\n    if [[ -n \"${REDIS_PID:-}\" ]] && kill -0 \"$REDIS_PID\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      kill \"$REDIS_PID\" 2>/dev/null || true\n      wait \"$REDIS_PID\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    fi\n    REDIS_PID=\"\"\n    start_redis\n  elif [[ -n \"${REDIS_PID:-}\" ]] && ! kill -0 \"$REDIS_PID\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    # We started redis but pid is gone while PING still works (adopted) — clear pid.\n    if redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING 2>/dev/null | grep -q PONG; then\n      REDIS_PID=\"\"\n    else\n      log \"Redis process exited; restarting\"\n      start_redis\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # HTTP nodes\n  local_id=0\n  for port in 8000 8001 8002; do\n    pid=\"${NODE_PIDS[$local_id]:-}\"\n    if [[ -z \"$pid\" ]] || ! kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      log \"Node $local_id (port $port) is down; restarting\"\n      start_node \"$local_id\" \"$port\"\n    fi\n    local_id=$((local_id + 1))\n  done\n\n  sleep 1\ndone\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":187,"fileSize":4746,"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/frontend-dev-1/start.sh","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":187},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-4\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_1","startedAtMs":"1787424978764","completedAtMs":"1787424980176"},"model_call_id":"e1004229-730f-4840-966d-b932d594bc6c-1-366j","session_id":"49ffb699-fd37-4b50-96be-46bad2e3f892","timestamp_ms":1787424980198}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-5\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_2","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"git log --oneline -10 -- start.sh; echo '---'; git status; echo '---'; git log --oneline -5; echo '---comments raw---'; loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null | head -c 2000; loom data comments MARATHON-21 2>/dev/null || true; loom data show MARATHON-21 2>&1 | head -80","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-52ea18d7-705c-4f59-83cc-6706705083ea-5\nfc_cdd28b7f-4b12-9e7f-9973-3017f0247761_2","simpleCommands":["git","echo","git","echo","git","echo","loom","python3","head","loom","true","loom","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"log"},{"type":"word","value":"--oneline"},{"type":"number","value":"-10"},{"type":"word","value":"--"},{"type":"word","value":"start.sh"}],"fullText":"git log --oneline -10 -- start.sh"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"status"}],"fullText":"git status"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"log"},{"type":"word","value":"--oneline"},{"type":"number","value":"-5"}],"fullText":"git log --oneline -5"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---comments raw---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---comments raw---'"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-m"},{"type":"word","value":"json.tool"}],"fullText":"python3 -m json.tool"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"2000"}],"fullText":"head -c 2000"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"comments"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"}],"fullText":"loom data comments MARATHON-21"},{"name":"true","args":[],"fullText":"true"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-21"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-21"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-80"}],"fullText":"head -80"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Git history and task comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"49ffb699-fd37-4b50-96be-46bad2e3f892","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"git log --oneline -10 -- start.sh; echo '---'; git status; echo '---'; git log --oneline -5; echo '---comments raw---'; loom data show MARATHON-21 --output json | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null | head -c 2000; loom data comments MARATHON-21 2>/dev/null || true; loom data show MARATHON-21 2>&1 | head -80","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"70903a1 Add Huddle cluster scaffold: start.sh, 3 nodes, Redis, health (MARATHON-2)\n---\nOn branch agents/MARATHON/frontend-dev-1\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\tloom-prompts/\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n---\ne328261 Track .gitignore for venv/data runtime artifacts (MARATHON-2)\n70903a1 Add Huddle cluster scaffold: start.sh, 3 nodes, Redis, health (MARATHON-2)\nadb99cc marathon baseline\n---comments raw---\n{\n    \"id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n    \"title\": \"HTTP node auto-restart within 60s\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": 0,\n    \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n    \"assignee\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n    \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n    \"labels\": [\n        \"backend\"\n    ],\n    \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n    \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n    \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nGuarantee that `/app/start.sh` (repo-root `start.sh`) automatically respawns any HTTP node that exits for any reason\\u2014including SIGKILL\\u2014so that `127.0.0.1:8000`, `:8001`, and `:8002` each answer `GET /api/health` again within **60 seconds wall-clock**, with **no external action**. Surviving nodes must keep serving throughout. MARATHON-2 already shipped a foreground supervisor and a 1s poll loop; this task owns the **hard 60s SLA**, death-detection/reap correctness, bind-retry behavior, and acceptance criteria for HTTP-only chaos. Redis respawn remains as designed in MARATHON-2 and must not regress, but is not the graded focus here.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n**Decision:** Harden the existing bash supervisor in `start.sh`\\u2014do not introduce systemd, supervisord, Docker, a second process manager, or an in-Python watchdog. Detection stays PID-based (children started by `start.sh`); readiness for the SLA is HTTP-based (`GET /api/health` \\u2192 200 on that port).\\n\\n**Why**\\n- The product and MARATHON-2 already lock three OS processes + bash ownership of lifecycle; rewriting supervision would break the epic\\u2019s ops seam.\\n- A poll interval of ~1s (or event-driven `wait -n` plus a short sleep) easily meets a 60s budget if death is detected and respawn does not abort the supervisor.\\n- Health readiness (not merely \\u201cPID exists\\u201d) matches how the grader and clients observe recovery.\\n\\n**Alternatives considered**\\n1. **Leave MARATHON-2 loop unchanged** \\u2014 notes claim ~2s recovery, but this P0 task exists as a dedicated graded slice; without explicit reap, bind-retry, and \\u201csupervisor must not exit on child The 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\ntime=2026-08-22T18:56:20.244Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:35473\nID:       MARATHON-21\nTitle:    HTTP node auto-restart within 60s\nStatus:   in_progress\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nAssignee: frontend-dev-1\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [backend]\n\nDescription:\nstart.sh must respawn any SIGKILLed HTTP node within 60s without external action so all three ports answer again. Surviving nodes keep serving during outage.\n\nDesign (--design):\n## Summary\n\nGuarantee that `/app/start.sh` (repo-root `start.sh`) automatically respawns any HTTP node that exits for any reason—including SIGKILL—so that `127.0.0.1:8000`, `:8001`, and `:8002` each answer `GET /api/health` again within **60 seconds wall-clock**, with **no external action**. Surviving nodes must keep serving throughout. MARATHON-2 already shipped a foreground supervisor and a 1s poll loop; this task owns the **hard 60s SLA**, death-detection/reap correctness, bind-retry behavior, and acceptance criteria for HTTP-only chaos. Redis respawn remains as designed in MARATHON-2 and must not regress, but is not the graded focus here.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n**Decision:** Harden the existing bash supervisor in `start.sh`—do not introduce systemd, supervisord, Docker, a second process manager, or an in-Python watchdog. Detection stays PID-based (children started by `start.sh`); readiness for the SLA is HTTP-based (`GET /api/health` → 200 on that port).\n\n**Why**\n- The product and MARATHON-2 already lock three OS processes + bash ownership of lifecycle; rewriting supervision would break the epic’s ops seam.\n- A poll interval of ~1s (or event-driven `wait -n` plus a short sleep) easily meets a 60s budget if death is detected and respawn does not abort the supervisor.\n- Health readiness (not merely “PID exists”) matches how the grader and clients observe recovery.\n\n**Alternatives considered**\n1. **Leave MARATHON-2 loop unchanged** — notes claim ~2s recovery, but this P0 task exists as a dedicated graded slice; without explicit reap, bind-retry, and “supervisor must not exit on child death” rules, implementers can leave latent races. Rejected as “design = no-op.”\n2. **External process manager (systemd user unit, supervisord)** — violates self-contained `/app/start.sh` foreground contract. Rejected.\n3. **In-process multi-port single OS process** — fails SIGKILL-one-node model. Rejected (already rejected in MARATHON-2).\n4. **Health-only probing without PID tracking** — can false-positive during slow starts and does not reap zombies; usable only as a secondary signal. Rejected as primary detector.\n\n**Trade-off accepted:** Brief connection failures on the killed port during the outage window are expected; clients must retry (SPA/WebSocket reconnect owned by later tasks). The supervisor optimizes for simple, local PID+poll reliability rather than zero-downtime migrate.\n\n**Consistency with MARATHON-2 (authoritative sibling)**\n- Keep port↔`node_id` map: `8000→0`, `8001→1`, `8002→2`.\n- Keep env: `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_HOST`, `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`.\n- Keep `GET /api/health` body `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}` unchanged.\n- MARATHON-2 text said “do not defer HTTP auto-restart to a later task”; the harness nonetheless created MARATHON-21. **This design does not diverge on mechanism**—it narrows ownership: MARATHON-21 is the SLA/hardening of the HTTP restart path already sketched in MARATHON-2, not a second supervisor.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Ops seam (verifier / QA ↔ `start.sh`) — **primary contract for this task**\n\n| Concern | Contract |\n|---|---|\n| Entrypoint | Executable `start.sh` at app root (`/app/start.sh` in runtime layout). |\n| Lifetime | Stays in the **foreground** until SIGINT/SIGTERM (or equivalent stop). |\n| HTTP children | Exactly three node processes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002` with stable `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`/`HUDDLE_PORT`. |\n| Auto-restart | If any HTTP child exits (SIGKILL, SIGTERM, crash, bind failure exit), `start.sh` respawns **that** node only, same id/port, without operator intervention. |\n| SLA | From the moment the process is gone, wall-clock time until `curl`/`GET http://127.0.0.1:<port>/api/health` returns **200** with correct `node_id` is **≤ 60s**. Target remains a few seconds. |\n| Survivors | While one port is down, the other two must continue to return 200 health (and any later APIs already mounted). |\n| Shutdown | SIGINT/SIGTERM to `start.sh` still tears down children (MARATHON-2); restart loop must not treat intentional shutdown as a respawn storm after trap runs. |\n\n**Ownership:** Backend / ops only. No frontend change in this task.\n\n### HTTP seam — `GET /api/health` (unchanged from MARATHON-2)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| Server (each node) | Return `200` `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":<0\\|1\\|2>}` when the process is listening; do not probe Redis/SQLite. |\n| Client (grader, future SPA) | Treat TCP refuse / timeout / non-200 as “this node down”; **retry**. Do not require all three nodes for reads that can hit a live peer. |\n| While killed node is down | Clients using that port see connection errors; clients on surviving ports are unaffected. |\n| After respawn | Same port, same `node_id`; no session stickiness invented here. |\n\n**Validation:** Server validates `HUDDLE_*` at process start (existing `huddle/config.py`). Client validates HTTP status + JSON keys for health checks.\n\n**Slow / fail behavior:** No new API errors. Outage is a transport failure, not an application error body.\n\n### Frontend / realtime seam (informational; not implemented here)\n\n| Consumer | Expected behavior during single-node kill |\n|---|---|\n| Future SPA (MARATHON-24+) | If its API base URL points at the dead port, show retry/reconnect; do not assume cluster-wide outage. |\n| WebSocket (MARATHON-20) | Connection on dead node drops; resume/subscribe against a live node is that task’s problem. Restart only restores a peer process. |\n| Cross-node fan-out (MARATHON-22) | May see a peer gap until respawn; must not require this task to change pub/sub code. |\n\nPayload shapes crossing the FE/BE JSON seam are **unchanged** by this task.\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T18:56:20.208Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:35473\n","executionTime":124,"interleavedOutput":"70903a1 Add Huddle cluster scaffold: start.sh, 3 nodes, Redis, health (MARATHON-2)\n---\nOn branch agents/MARATHON/frontend-dev-1\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\tloom-prompts/\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n---\ne328261 Track .gitignore for venv/data runtime artifacts (MARATHON-2)\n70903a1 Add Huddle cluster scaffold: start.sh, 3 nodes, Redis, health (MARATHON-2)\nadb99cc marathon baseline\n---comments raw---\ntime=2026-08-22T18:56:20.208Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:35473\n{\n    \"id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n    \"title\": \"HTTP node auto-restart within 60s\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": 0,\n    \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n    \"assignee\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n    \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n    \"labels\": [\n        \"backend\"\n    ],\n    \"sourc